   "title": "\u8bf4\u660e",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "viggle-animate-h3 - one node that turns a driving clip plus one still into a video latent.\n\nFeed it:\n  video            frames of the driving clip (Load Video -> IMAGE), 24 fps\n  audio            the same clip audio; it also goes straight to the save node\n  reference_image  ONE still of the person or character to place into the clip\n                   (a repainted frame from the same shot works best)\n  model / vae      stock ComfyUI loaders: Load Diffusion Model -> Load LoRA, Load VAE\n\nInside it builds the Viggle-Animate conditioning and runs the sampler, then hands back the video\nlatent: decode with MiniMax-H3 VAE Decode, save with VHS_VideoCombine.\n\nDefaults are the evaluated configuration: 6 steps, 124 frames, flow shift 3/3.\nAttention is routed automatically per call - sol_attn while the three contiguous q/k/v copies fit,\ndense beyond that - see the project page for the measurements."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "viggle-animate-h3:\u6743\u91cd\u3001LoRA\u3001VAE \u5168\u90e8\u7528 ComfyUI \u81ea\u5e26\u7684\u52a0\u8f7d\u5668\u8282\u70b9,\u8fde\u7ebf\u9001\u8fdb\u672c\u8282\u70b9\u3002\n  1. \u5de6\u8fb9\u653e\u9a71\u52a8\u89c6\u9891(\u753b\u9762\u548c\u58f0\u97f3)\u548c\u53c2\u8003\u56fe(\u6700\u597d\u662f\u540c\u4e00\u955c\u5934\u91cc\u6539\u7ed8\u7684\u4e00\u5e27)\n  2. \u70b9 Run\n  3. \u53f3\u8fb9 VHS_VideoCombine \u51fa mp4(\u5e26\u9a71\u52a8\u89c6\u9891\u539f\u58f0)\n\n\u8fde\u7ebf:Load Diffusion Model -> Load LoRA -> \u8282\u70b9 model;Load VAE -> \u8282\u70b9 vae \u548c VAE Decode;\n\u9a71\u52a8\u89c6\u9891 IMAGE/audio -> \u8282\u70b9 video/audio;\u53c2\u8003\u56fe -> reference_image;\n\u8282\u70b9 latent -> VAE Decode -> \u4fdd\u5b58\u8282\u70b9;\u8282\u70b9 audio \u76f4\u901a\u4fdd\u5b58\u8282\u70b9\u3002\n\u8282\u70b9\u91cc\u53ea\u7559 slimdit \u81ea\u5df1\u7684\u8bbe\u7f6e:\u6b65\u6570 3/4/6\u3001\u5e27\u6570\u3001seed\u3001\u6587\u672c\u6761\u4ef6\u3001shift\u3002"
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
